id=a52sxq_wifi_watchdog
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Wi-Fi data-path watchdog
author=kusti420
description=Self-heal for Wi-Fi "connected, no internet": when the default route is on wlan0, the gateway stays unresolvable (ARP FAILED/INCOMPLETE) and packets go out but none come in for 20 s, /system/bin/k4-wifiwatch re-evaluates the network (cellular takes over at once) and restarts Wi-Fi for a new association (twice at most), then stays quiet for 10 minutes. Android itself never recovers from this state: NetworkStack (Android 16+) ignores NUD failures of a gateway that was never reachable in the session, so there is no reconnect, and Samsung's WifiConnectivityMonitor is disabled on this port. Also sets, once per device, Settings.Global network_avoid_bad_wifi=1 (Samsung's CSC default is 0 = stay on a Wi-Fi without internet; with 1 a validated mobile network takes over meanwhile; marker persist.sys.k4.wifiwatch_defaults). Opt-out of the watchdog: setprop persist.sys.k4.wifiwatch 0. Status in sys.k4.wifiwatch and the kernel log.
